          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Rudyard Kipling</strong><br>\nRudyard Kipling was born in Bombay, India, on December 30, 1865, during the British Raj, to English parents. His early years in India, surrounded by exotic sights and sounds, deeply influenced his later writing. At age six, he was sent to England for schooling but faced harsh treatment in foster care until his time at the United Services College, which was a happier period for him.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Return to India and Early Work</strong><br>\nIn 1882, Kipling returned to India and worked for seven years as a journalist. He started his literary career by publishing stories in newspapers and magazines, with his experiences in colonial India providing rich material for his early works. His vivid portrayals of the Indian Subcontinent left a permanent mark on English literature.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Kipling's Literary Breakthrough</strong><br>\nKipling's literary breakthrough came with the publication of \"Plain Tales from the Hills\" in 1888. This collection of short stories gained popularity for its insightful look into the lives and dynamics of British and Indian society in colonial India. His use of colloquial language brought his stories to life for many readers.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
